reBART - third-party notices
=============================

reBART is licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE). It re-implements
techniques and interoperates with the projects below. No source code from the
MIT projects was copied, only documented facts (register numbers), a shared
NVRAM variable for interop, and reverse-engineered hardware behavior were used.

- PCI Express Base Specification
    The Resizable BAR capability register numbers used in the driver are facts
    defined by this specification.

- xCuri0/ReBarUEFI  (MIT)   https://github.com/xCuri0/ReBarUEFI
    reBART uses the same "ReBarState" NVRAM variable name and GUID so that the
    ReBarState.exe tool from this project can control it. No code copied.
    (Note: ReBarUEFI's own pciRegs.h is GPL-2.0/Linux and is NOT used or
    included here; reBART defines its own constants from the PCIe spec.)

- terminatorul/NvStrapsReBar  (MIT)   https://github.com/terminatorul/NvStrapsReBar
    The Turing BAR-size strap method (BAR0 MMIO strap window, commit bit) was
    re-implemented from this project's reverse-engineering. No code copied.

- EDK2 / TianoCore  (BSD-2-Clause-Patent)   https://github.com/tianocore/edk2
    reBART is built as an EDK2 DXE driver and uses EDK2 headers and libraries.
